{
 "_doc": "RACE - the round screen for the track. The watchdog guards only RPM over (shift at 6200, over-rev at 6500) and coolant over (105, critical 112) and never draws over a screen (show_popup false): they show on the lamp strip (SHIFT, OVER-REV, ENGINE HOT, always up) and by bringing their screens up - the big tach at over-rev, the coolant gauge when hot. Rules: the timers at a standstill with the engine above 2500 rpm (a launch), the G-meter under hard braking (-0.7 g). Oil pressure and charging still pop up: losing either on a track ends the engine. Shift points are for a petrol EJ with a 6500 redline - set yours. Network: only its AP name (Telemetry-Gauge-Race), so it is told apart from the daily screen; its channel and password stay the display's own.",
